From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0101] anv/nvmtl, xemac: rename B580 to IntelXe

On top of the whole series as installed (prod9, mesa/b580-prod9.diff before this rename); the result is
mesa/intelxe.diff.

The kernel extension is IntelXe.kext now: it was named after the first card it drove, and it is meant for Intel Xe
GPUs. Its uAPI extensions follow the name: uapi/b580_drm.h is intelxe_drm.h, DRM_IOCTL_B580_* / DRM_B580_* are
DRM_IOCTL_INTELXE_* / DRM_INTELXE_*, B580_CAP_* / B580_SURFACE_* are INTELXE_CAP_* / INTELXE_SURFACE_*, struct
drm_b580_* is struct drm_intelxe_*. Ioctl numbers, capability values and structure layouts are unchanged, so this
build talks to the same kernel interface; only the names differ. Comments name IntelXe.kext and debug.intelxe.*.

The header was included by a path relative to the Mesa checkout ("../../../../b580/uapi/b580_drm.h", the layout of the
development tree). It is now found through the xemac dependency: <xemac>/../uapi is an include directory, the place
xemac.c already takes it from (in the intel-gpu-macos-driver repository user/uapi, a link to kernel/IntelXe/uapi).
---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 3e20988..0c8b70f 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -824,7 +824,8 @@ if with_xemac
   _xemac_dir = get_option('xemac')
   files_xemac = files(_xemac_dir / 'xemac.c', _xemac_dir / 'xemac_drm.c')
   dep_libdrm = declare_dependency(
-    include_directories : include_directories(_xemac_dir, _xemac_dir / 'libdrm'),
+    # <xemac>/../uapi: the kernel's uAPI headers (intelxe_drm.h), where xemac.c finds them too
+    include_directories : include_directories(_xemac_dir, _xemac_dir / 'libdrm', _xemac_dir / '..' / 'uapi'),
   )
   pre_args += '-DHAVE_XEMAC'
 endif
